  "observations": [
    "The AFM objective, cantilever tip and docked sample share the inspected optical axis. The lower barrel clears the holder and the sample puck has a connected visible support.",
    "The docked and returned AFM frames recover the same workfield. The withdrawn drawer permits holder service; the recessed door handle still stows and deploys.",
    "Nikon, Zeiss and probe working areas retain their optical orientation and supported stages. The corrected stand, specimen holder and clamp details remain present in the delivered models.",
    "Transfer and bonder focus supports are distinct from their moving optical housings. The transfer handwheel, vertical adjuster and camera cable retain the previously repaired clearances.",
    "The existing table and metal reflections remain visible. The shared lighting/reflection modules are unchanged; Photo inspection captures retain low-sample noise.",
    "Tweezers retain their existing geometry, supported by a fresh measured pickup/placement clearance audit. No unsupported cosmetic change was made solely to mark the asset changed."
  ],
